      "notes": "Montages, captions and native complete diagrams reviewed. Native38 confirms the complete seventeen-piece final board after Ne5: White Kg2/Ra1/Nb1/Bf2/a2/b2/c3/g3/h2 against Kg8/Rd1/Ne5/a7/b7/e2/g7/h7, White to move. This later position differs from native33: the king has moved from h1 to g2, the bishop from g1 to f2, the knight from c6 to e5, and the pawn from e4 to e2. Independent Na3/Rxa1 illustrates the rook capture after the b1 knight moves. Independent h3/e1=Q/Bxe1/Rxe1 legally exchanges the new queen and bishop and leaves fifteen pieces; e1=Q is not check against Kg2. These are explicitly supplied analysis comparisons, not a remembered game continuation or certified win. All ten source pawns are accounted for through the actual promotion and captures. The narrator says the original friendly-game ending was not recorded or remembered; do not invent it. Complete outcomes for all White defenses, the earlier overloaded-bishop sequence and the resulting larger conversions remain pending. Source images and captions exist; previous seventeen-piece draft and review history preserved.",
